audCC:'"[{\"start\":0,\"editorState\":{\"blocks\":[{\"key\":\"7c0e5\",\"text\":\"You choose emotionally unstable, so your next choice becomes one of the following. The first choice is that Hamlet is collapsing under the weight of his own emotions. The theme of grief is clear here and it turns Hamlet’s soliloquy into a cry for help. It’s no wonder that Hamlet is paralyzed by indecision. The second choice is that Hamlet is overwhelmed by competing outside influences – the Ghost’s need for Hamlet to avenge him, Ophelia’s desire to be in a relationship, Claudius watching his every move, and Gertrude’s appeal for him to abandon his grief and return to normal life. This speaks to the weight of expectations. Who does Hamlet owe allegiance to: himself or to others? Can outside pressure drive you mad?\",\"type\":\"unstyled\",\"depth\":0,\"inlineStyleRanges\":[{\"offset\":0,\"length\":722,\"style\":\"textHighlightEnable:false\"},{\"offset\":0,\"length\":722,\"style\":\"textTransform:none\"},{\"offset\":0,\"length\":722,\"style\":\"textShadowOpacity:none\"},{\"offset\":0,\"length\":722,\"style\":\"overridden:true\"},{\"offset\":0,\"length\":722,\"style\":\"textDecoration:none\"},{\"offset\":0,\"length\":722,\"style\":\"borderBottomStyle:none\"},{\"offset\":0,\"length\":722,\"style\":\"textShadowEnable:false\"},{\"offset\":0,\"length\":722,\"style\":\"hlnk:\"},{\"offset\":0,\"length\":722,\"style\":\"textShadowBlur:8px\"},{\"offset\":0,\"length\":722,\"style\":\"desktop-fontSize:24\"},{\"offset\":0,\"length\":722,\"style\":\"hlnke:true\"},{\"offset\":0,\"length\":722,\"style\":\"WebkitTextStrokeWidth:1px\"},{\"offset\":0,\"length\":722,\"style\":\"hlnkt:wp\"},{\"offset\":0,\"length\":722,\"style\":\"fontStyle:normal\"},{\"offset\":0,\"length\":722,\"style\":\"fontFamily:Raleway\"},{\"offset\":0,\"length\":722,\"style\":\"defaultTextStrokeWidth:1px\"},{\"offset\":0,\"length\":722,\"style\":\"mobile-fontSize:24\"},{\"offset\":0,\"length\":722,\"style\":\"WebkitTextStrokeColor:#F1EEE6\"},{\"offset\":0,\"length\":722,\"style\":\"fontWeight:400\"},{\"offset\":0,\"length\":722,\"style\":\"textOutlineEnable:false\"},{\"offset\":0,\"length\":722,\"style\":\"opacity:1\"},{\"offset\":0,\"length\":722,\"style\":\"defaultTextStrokeColor:#F1EEE6\"},{\"offset\":0,\"length\":722,\"style\":\"defaultTextShadow:none\"},{\"offset\":0,\"length\":722,\"style\":\"backgroundColor:unset\"},{\"offset\":0,\"length\":722,\"style\":\"tablet-fontSize:24\"},{\"offset\":0,\"length\":722,\"style\":\"textShadow:none\"},{\"offset\":0,\"length\":722,\"style\":\"textShadowX:0px\"},{\"offset\":0,\"length\":722,\"style\":\"fontStretch:normal\"},{\"offset\":0,\"length\":722,\"style\":\"fontType:regular\"},{\"offset\":0,\"length\":722,\"style\":\"color:#ffffff\"},{\"offset\":0,\"length\":722,\"style\":\"defaultBackgroundColor:#E8D01B\"},{\"offset\":0,\"length\":722,\"style\":\"textShadowY:4px\"},{\"offset\":0,\"length\":722,\"style\":\"textShadowColor:#F1EEE61F\"},{\"offset\":0,\"length\":722,\"style\":\"lineHeight:135%\"},{\"offset\":0,\"length\":722,\"style\":\"letterSpacing:0%\"}],\"entityRanges\":[],\"data\":{\"listDepth\":\"0\",\"listColor\":\"#666666\",\"listIndent\":\"100%\",\"verticalAlign\":\"middle\",\"overridden\":\"true\",\"marginLeft\":\"0px\",\"listType\":\"S_Bullets08\",\"textAlign\":\"center\",\"marginBottom\":\"0%\",\"presetId\":\"text-closedcaptions\",\"listSize\":\"100%\"}}],\"entityMap\":{}},\"CCPosition\":\"BOTTOM\",\"text\":\"You choose emotionally unstable, so your next choice becomes one of the following. The first choice is that Hamlet is collapsing under the weight of his own emotions. The theme of grief is clear here and it turns Hamlet’s soliloquy into a cry for help. It’s no wonder that Hamlet is paralyzed by indecision. The second choice is that Hamlet is overwhelmed by competing outside influences – the Ghost’s need for Hamlet to avenge him, Ophelia’s desire to be in a relationship, Claudius watching his every move, and Gertrude’s appeal for him to abandon his grief and return to normal life. This speaks to the weight of expectations. Who does Hamlet owe allegiance to: himself or to others? Can outside pressure drive you mad?\",\"duration\":51.7,\"end\":51.7,\"id\":\"caption__2207__24\",\"dirtyReasons\":[],\"speechAgentV1\":{\"name\":\"Nathaniel C. - Natural Conversations\",\"voiceId\":{\"uid\":\"lnIpQcZuikKim3oNdYlP\",\"modelId\":\"1\"},\"source\":\"AIVoices\"}}]"',
